# Coding constraints (core packages)

Match Prettier: `semi: false`, `singleQuote: true`, `arrowParens: "avoid"`.

## Forbidden in ESLint-enforced core packages

- `const enum` (use non-const enums; build inlines them)
- Object rest/spread (use `extend` from `@vue/shared`)
- Optional chaining
- `async` / `await`

Prefer `slice` over `substring`. Use `import type`. Prefer `@ts-expect-error` over `@ts-ignore`.

## Environment

Most packages are env-agnostic — do not use `window`, `document`, or `require` outside DOM/Node-targeted packages (see `eslint.config.js` overrides).

## Flags and DCE

Use `packages/global.d.ts` constants (`__DEV__`, `__TEST__`, `__BROWSER__`, `__SSR__`, `__FEATURE_*`, …):

- Gate warnings / expensive diagnostics with `__DEV__`.
- Export DEV-only surface as `(__DEV__ ? impl : NOOP)` when required.
- Keep optional subsystems behind `__FEATURE_*`.
- Never leak compiler-only or DEV-only code into runtime prod builds.

## Errors

- Runtime: `warn()`, `callWithErrorHandling` / `callWithAsyncErrorHandling`, `ErrorCodes`
- Compiler: `createCompilerError` via `context.onError` / `onWarn`; `assert()` for internals
- Public API via `src/index.ts`; mark internals with `/** @internal */`
